## Run it

| | |
|---|---|
| Start | `uv run python harness.py` |
| Check without Slack | `uv run python harness.py --once --dry-run --no-slack` |
| Check it end to end | `uv run python harness.py --verify-plan`, then `docs/verify.md` |
| Is it running, is Slack on | `STATUS.md` (regenerated every tick) |
| What it did and what waits for you | `HEARTBEAT.md` |
| Run log | `logs/harness.jsonl`, earlier days in `logs/harness.<date>.jsonl.gz` |

## Stopping it on purpose

<!-- Fill this in if the harness runs all the time (bin/ops-kit.py, docs/operations.md);
     otherwise leave the first row and delete the second. With a watchdog the order
     matters: stopped the other way round, it is running again within two minutes. -->

| To | Run |
|---|---|
| Stop it for a while | Ctrl-C in its terminal, or `scripts/…-up down` (the watchdog leaves it down until `scripts/…-up`) |
| Take it down for good | Remove the watchdog first (`launchctl bootout …` / `systemctl --user disable --now …`), then `scripts/…-up down` |

